{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0004","source_sha256":"8d3450572d1b6869b04b67cedd84ffa4f9258006ea918c1c986b69ac02f170c7","independent_option":3,"reasoning_summary":"Solving 1/(n+6) < 3/20 < 1/(n+1) yields 20 < 3n+18 and 3n+3 < 20, so 2/3 < n < 17/3. Thus n in {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"solver","independent_context":true,"blockers":[]}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0008","source_sha256":"528fd64f0f0229d74ed0610a82c7acd8850f9a53f2a810455edd9654f196c0ab","independent_option":1,"reasoning_summary":"The universal set is the union of A and A'. If the universal set is infinite and A is finite, A' must be infinite.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"solver","independent_context":true,"blockers":[]}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0009","source_sha256":"ff15f9d648b5a1f22a71d15d7d1acca714563397194e5c4a44df8d72e80633d5","independent_option":2,"reasoning_summary":"If A is finite, A' is infinite. The union of an infinite set A' and any set B is infinite.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"solver","independent_context":true,"blockers":[]}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0010","source_sha256":"f836e17cc393e9107227f6be26ecbbe6e4a41a4f04aa997e4a05fad581fb98a2","independent_option":2,"reasoning_summary":"Since A U B' is finite, A must be finite. A - B is a subset of A, so it must also be finite.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"solver","independent_context":true,"blockers":[]}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0011","source_sha256":"e5583b32259c0f2a57b63669cf9b406f5a33624878001c6e367cd5482cf43a97","independent_option":3,"reasoning_summary":"Since A is a subset of B, A - B is the empty set. The complement of the empty set is the universal set, which is infinite because B is infinite.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"solver","independent_context":true,"blockers":[]}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0013","source_sha256":"6876a412eea14c32184bdeb72c60372e6a95238e7f6fb9b2dfa505fc1034a6e5","independent_option":1,"reasoning_summary":"The set difference A - B being empty means there are no elements in A that are not in B, which is the definition of A being a subset of B.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"solver","independent_context":true,"blockers":[]}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0061","source_sha256":"8afe58fcd754e8f0c3dbb2fa6fbbcbeebadc77fabf6ee7ad1715b896c529d251","independent_option":3,"reasoning_summary":"The common difference d = (10 - 4) / (10 - 6) = 1.5. The 16th term is a_10 + 6d = 10 + 6(1.5) = 19.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"solver","independent_context":true,"blockers":[]}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0063","source_sha256":"675c4f9d52888b8054b369ab0b75b6b1d6a9e02e2cfa73283b644f146964d5ce","independent_option":2,"reasoning_summary":"The common difference d = (7 - 18) / (18 - 7) = -1. The nth term is a_7 + (n-7)d = 18 - (n-7) = 25 - n. Setting to zero gives n = 25.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"solver","independent_context":true,"blockers":[]}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0064","source_sha256":"ee7e16326178691231aa3e00f2e82f89d1852d98bb40a7434b48763ec207db95","independent_option":3,"reasoning_summary":"In an arithmetic sequence, 2a_{n-1} = a_n + a_{n-2}. Therefore, a_{n-2} = a_7, and since it is non-constant, n - 2 = 7, giving n = 9.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"solver","independent_context":true,"blockers":[]}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0065","source_sha256":"a6f4a93ceb551812507b94917596bca7e83da0c6de5392c1d91a8dfb05687e85","independent_option":4,"reasoning_summary":"We have a_1 + 26d = 2(a_1 + 17d), yielding a_1 = -8d. Thus, a_n = -8d + (n-1)d = (n-9)d. Setting a_n to zero with d != 0 gives n = 9.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"solver","independent_context":true,"blockers":[]}
